# Planned on bare metal on an 8745HS (Zen 4, full AVX-512): W0WWV at the
# WWV site, RAC 19, Debian 13 (kernel 6.12.117).  FFTW 3.3.11 built with
# avx512 (Phil's /usr/local build; header "fftw-3.3.11 ... avx512"), so
# this file is only accepted by a radiod linked to a 3.3.11
# sse2-avx-avx2-avx2_128-avx512 libfftw3f -- Debian/Ubuntu's 3.3.10
# packages reject it and plan from scratch as before.  Laid out the way
# sigmond runs radiod: radiod's pair = CPUs 7+15 at 3200 MHz (performance,
# measured 3169 MHz via APERF/MPERF), every other CPU capped at 1400 MHz,
# xhci IRQs on 0,8, no resctrl/CAT (radiod_l3_bytes is the sysfs L3
# domain; harvest guessed "guest" for want of resctrl).  Whole station
# stopped by `smd admin wisdom suspend`.  `smd admin wisdom plan --fresh`
# = `taskset -c 7 fftwf-wisdom -v -T 1 -n` (nothing imported) over 161
# specs: sigmond's 151 profiles + 10 from radiod's fft.log.  853 plans;
# 2 h 5 m 59 s (2026-11-23 04:17:52Z - 06:23:51Z).  In production the
# rof3240000 fft thread uses 31.3% of CPU 7 at 3169 MHz (32.2% with the
# Oct 6 wisdom it replaced; the Zen 3 5825U on Debian's 3.3.10 sse2-avx
# FFTW uses ~45% at 3381 MHz).
